      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Which of the following best describes the projection of the intersection between the elliptic cone ${x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}=2{z}^{2}$ and the plane $2z-x+1=0$ onto the $xy$-plane?",
      "worked_solution": "Since we want to find the projection onto the $xy$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $z.$ First, we solve the equation of the plane for $z,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n2z-x+1=0\\,⟹\\,z=\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $z$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2} & =2{(\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+3{y}^{2} & =2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\ {x}^{2}+3{y}^{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-x+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+x+3{y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}(x+1)^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}+3{y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{2}+3{y}^{2} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of an ellipse centered at $(-1,0)$ in the $xy$-plane.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
